cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this protocol or the scripts, please cite it as below."
title: "A protocol for verifying ecological analysis code developed with AI assistance"
abstract: >-
  A protocol for verifying scientific analysis code and for reporting that
  verification, with the scripts and prompts used to carry it out. Part A
  establishes that reported numbers came from a documented run that does not
  depend on the session, the machine, or the moment it was produced. Part B
  enumerates every transformation on the path to a reported number and checks
  each one. Includes two R scripts for running and comparing verification runs,
  and two prompts for the steps that may be delegated to a language model.
type: software
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - code verification
  - scientific computing
  - large language models
  - ecology
  - R
authors:
  - family-names: Fujiwara
    given-names: Masami
    affiliation: "Department of Ecology and Conservation Biology, Texas A&M University"
